WEBVTT

00:00:18.614 --> 00:00:27.144
Kanashimi ikuta noseshi fune

00:00:29.124 --> 00:00:39.334
Horobi no uta no koe takaku

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:48.664
Kuraki soko yori

00:00:50.114 --> 00:00:55.214
Ukabi koshi

00:00:59.184 --> 00:01:10.324
Aa kimi to ima shirogane o nuke

00:01:11.134 --> 00:01:22.074
Ozora e futari tobu hi no

00:01:22.074 --> 00:01:36.254
Kuru o yume min, kuru o yume min

00:01:43.704 --> 00:01:45.604
Maybe you should lie down...

00:01:45.664 --> 00:01:46.994
Don't touch me!

00:01:48.204 --> 00:01:51.034
What's with you, anyway?

00:01:51.504 --> 00:01:57.374
Trying to throttle me, getting us put in the
same room... what're you trying to do?

00:01:57.714 --> 00:01:59.644
What do you want from me?

00:02:00.884 --> 00:02:03.644
I don't want anything from you!

00:02:04.954 --> 00:02:07.384
Is that so?

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:10.084
Well, I've got a few ideas of my own!

00:02:44.224 --> 00:02:45.824
Never...

00:02:45.824 --> 00:02:47.194
again...

00:03:35.774 --> 00:03:38.004
Well, good riddance!

00:03:39.514 --> 00:03:41.104
Uneasiness.

00:03:48.554 --> 00:03:51.854
I'm glad you're all right, Commander Ekaril.

00:03:52.964 --> 00:03:55.934
It's been quite a while, Master Commander.

00:03:57.904 --> 00:04:01.734
Now, please give us your account
of the details of the accident.

00:04:02.204 --> 00:04:07.664
I'd also like to know why you've been out of
communication for the past 20 Skoors.

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:12.844
This is the record of the accident.

00:04:14.284 --> 00:04:18.244
I apologize for the delay.

00:04:27.994 --> 00:04:30.464
Don't tell me you're having breakfast now!

00:04:30.664 --> 00:04:32.724
She's not even dressed!

00:04:33.104 --> 00:04:35.164
What a waste of a day off!

00:04:41.144 --> 00:04:43.844
We're going shopping today.

00:04:43.984 --> 00:04:45.384
Yeah!

00:04:45.384 --> 00:04:46.674
Oh?

00:04:49.214 --> 00:04:51.454
Forget her. Let's go!

00:04:51.454 --> 00:04:53.014
Yeah, what should we buy?

00:04:54.524 --> 00:04:56.044
Weirdoes...

00:05:06.134 --> 00:05:07.294
All right!

00:05:49.314 --> 00:05:50.384
Are you studying?

00:05:50.384 --> 00:05:52.314
I-I'm not doing anything!

00:05:52.314 --> 00:05:56.214
I just wanted to look something up! So I...

00:05:57.484 --> 00:05:58.744
Oh!

00:05:59.154 --> 00:06:00.624
It's you, Mari!

00:06:04.194 --> 00:06:06.854
The Emil Force Drive went berserk?

00:06:10.534 --> 00:06:13.534
You've been waiting for the ship to
restore its functions...

00:06:13.534 --> 00:06:16.564
And that's why you haven't been in contact?

00:06:18.904 --> 00:06:20.304
Yes.

00:06:20.474 --> 00:06:24.684
When the drive went berserk, the entire
landing force was annihilated,

00:06:24.684 --> 00:06:27.844
as well as one of the Blue's navigators.

00:06:29.284 --> 00:06:38.884
And at the destination point, 800 Forimes died
from the effects of the Emil Force Drive.

00:06:41.794 --> 00:06:44.794
I take responsibility for all of this.

00:06:44.934 --> 00:06:46.624
Obviously!

00:06:47.434 --> 00:06:49.704
Of course it's your responsibility!

00:06:54.874 --> 00:06:56.404
Stories?

00:06:59.614 --> 00:07:01.544
Ever since I was little...

00:07:01.984 --> 00:07:07.544
I loved it when anyone read me
picture books or told me stories.

00:07:07.854 --> 00:07:11.364
Mwa-ha-ha! Now you're going to be my bride!

00:07:11.364 --> 00:07:18.894
The wizard cast a spell on the princess.

00:07:20.234 --> 00:07:23.224
But just then, who should ap-p-

00:07:24.644 --> 00:07:31.604
But my parents were busy running their store,
so they didn't have time very often.

00:07:32.444 --> 00:07:36.614
Before long, I started making up my own stories.

00:07:37.054 --> 00:07:41.324
No! You mustn't do that for me!

00:07:41.324 --> 00:07:48.454
Princess! This is your chance to escape the
witch's curse! Then, you and I...

00:07:49.194 --> 00:07:56.194
I started to really enjoy making up stories, even
though I never showed them to anyone.

00:07:56.974 --> 00:07:58.404
To this day...

00:08:00.044 --> 00:08:02.804
Oh? What kind of stories?

00:08:04.644 --> 00:08:06.084
No!

00:08:06.084 --> 00:08:07.984
Not even you, Mari!

00:08:07.984 --> 00:08:11.884
For one thing, I've never shown them to anyone!

00:08:12.284 --> 00:08:15.254
Why not? You really should!

00:08:15.654 --> 00:08:17.684
I can't! I really can't!

00:08:19.224 --> 00:08:22.854
It's really nothing to be shy about...

00:08:24.134 --> 00:08:28.534
Please don't tell anyone about this!
It's a secret!

00:08:29.234 --> 00:08:30.674
Okay.

00:08:32.404 --> 00:08:39.784
I know it's strange. At school and in the dorm,
I can never seem to speak my mind.

00:08:40.214 --> 00:08:43.654
I can only really express myself in my stories!

00:08:45.124 --> 00:08:46.484
That's not true!

00:08:47.084 --> 00:08:49.354
It's like I'm running away from reality.

00:08:50.424 --> 00:08:52.514
I know it's pathetic...

00:08:57.034 --> 00:08:58.894
Running away?

00:08:59.734 --> 00:09:01.464
Yes, running away.

00:09:07.844 --> 00:09:09.574
Okay, I'm going now!

00:09:09.744 --> 00:09:12.504
Right! Happy thieving!

00:09:13.144 --> 00:09:14.584
Leave it to me!

00:09:25.824 --> 00:09:28.724
Youngsters these days...

00:09:29.534 --> 00:09:31.194
Hey, you two!

00:09:31.604 --> 00:09:38.244
Who cares how many Forime you killed,
you murderer?

00:09:38.244 --> 00:09:43.714
Two hundred of our compatriots died
in that landing force! And...

00:09:43.714 --> 00:09:47.844
Murderer?! Don't speak to the
commander that way!

00:09:49.214 --> 00:09:50.944
Stop, Azanael!

00:09:51.354 --> 00:09:58.054
And Onomil... How dare you lump Onomil
in with the likes of them!

00:09:59.524 --> 00:10:00.924
I won't...

00:10:02.264 --> 00:10:03.424
I won't tolerate it!

00:10:06.964 --> 00:10:08.434
I said, stop!

00:10:10.504 --> 00:10:11.974
You murderer!

00:10:12.044 --> 00:10:13.834
You killed them!

00:10:14.314 --> 00:10:16.074
Two hundred of our compatriots!

00:10:16.214 --> 00:10:17.834
And Onomil!

00:10:19.284 --> 00:10:21.214
Murderer!

00:10:41.674 --> 00:10:45.194
Um, Miss Kawashima? Where are we going?

00:10:45.874 --> 00:10:48.744
Just follow me. Hmm?

00:10:52.984 --> 00:10:54.104
What is it?

00:10:54.214 --> 00:10:56.584
There sure are a lot of empty shops.

00:10:56.754 --> 00:10:59.944
Yeah, this place has gotten pretty desolate.

00:11:00.854 --> 00:11:02.384
I'm sorry.

00:11:04.224 --> 00:11:05.754
How come you're apologizing?

00:11:06.364 --> 00:11:09.164
Oh... you're from this town, aren't you, Kozuki?

00:11:09.664 --> 00:11:13.994
Yes. It used to be a lot livelier...

00:11:14.204 --> 00:11:16.734
Nobody's blaming you.

00:11:16.734 --> 00:11:18.874
You shouldn't take every little thing to heart!

00:11:18.874 --> 00:11:19.904
Yes...

00:11:19.904 --> 00:11:21.464
Let's go.

00:11:21.714 --> 00:11:23.234
Hey, Wakatake!

00:11:23.414 --> 00:11:24.904
Wakatake!

00:11:26.544 --> 00:11:30.614
You're in for a delicious meal! So, cheer up!

00:11:38.424 --> 00:11:43.794
There was one Forime who was unaffected
by the Emil Force Drive?

00:11:43.794 --> 00:11:48.494
Yes. It's unclear why.
I'm still investigating the matter.

00:11:49.334 --> 00:11:54.174
Please do, Ekaril. And keep your spirits up.

00:11:54.644 --> 00:11:58.704
Thank you, Master Commander Shivariel.

00:12:10.254 --> 00:12:12.954
Ship Five departing for assigned area.

00:12:16.464 --> 00:12:19.264
This vessel will now return to Trench One.

00:12:21.374 --> 00:12:23.034
No... wait.

00:12:27.244 --> 00:12:29.474
I'm intrigued...

00:12:43.294 --> 00:12:44.364
It's delicious!

00:12:44.364 --> 00:12:45.394
Truly!

00:12:45.394 --> 00:12:46.564
Right?

00:12:46.564 --> 00:12:49.554
The chef here studied in France.

00:12:52.404 --> 00:12:54.024
Do you come here a lot?

00:12:54.774 --> 00:12:57.704
I never knew about this place!

00:12:58.344 --> 00:13:03.974
I come here whenever we have a day off, but I
still can't manage to steal their secrets.

00:13:05.414 --> 00:13:06.904
Steal?

00:13:07.214 --> 00:13:12.344
Yeah. The dorm chief says that
skills have to be stolen!

00:13:13.154 --> 00:13:22.354
She was going to come too, but has a bunch of
reports to do. She just couldn't make it!

00:13:28.774 --> 00:13:31.604
I think they're using balsamic vinegar...

00:13:32.644 --> 00:13:34.194
Such depth of flavor...

00:13:48.424 --> 00:13:50.014
That sure was delicious!

00:13:50.594 --> 00:13:52.824
You finally feel better?

00:13:53.424 --> 00:13:55.764
I wasn't feeling bad!

00:13:56.334 --> 00:14:00.964
Come to think of it, Mari, you haven't
been yourself since yesterday!

00:14:01.274 --> 00:14:03.104
That's not true!

00:14:03.634 --> 00:14:08.244
You're the one who was freaking out
about your stories, Michi!

00:14:08.244 --> 00:14:09.574
M-Mari!

00:14:09.574 --> 00:14:11.064
Oops.

00:14:11.514 --> 00:14:12.874
Stories?

00:14:18.954 --> 00:14:23.084
How dare she speak to you that way!

00:14:23.354 --> 00:14:24.584
It's fine.

00:14:25.694 --> 00:14:30.224
It's true... the accident was my responsibility.

00:14:30.804 --> 00:14:31.994
Commander!

00:14:36.004 --> 00:14:38.734
Ship 1 Novaal is mobilizing.

00:14:39.074 --> 00:14:43.474
Detecting launch of a small vessel.
An anti-personnel probe.

00:14:43.974 --> 00:14:45.374
Anti-personnel?

00:14:45.484 --> 00:14:46.914
Where's its destination?

00:14:47.044 --> 00:14:51.814
Probable destination: Western portion
of island chain near Trench Five.

00:15:00.294 --> 00:15:03.264
Well, well! You write stories, Kozuki?

00:15:05.664 --> 00:15:07.564
I'm sorry, Michi!

00:15:08.334 --> 00:15:09.964
Forget it.

00:15:14.004 --> 00:15:16.804
You know, I'd like to be a cook one day.

00:15:17.784 --> 00:15:19.334
A cook?

00:15:19.614 --> 00:15:23.884
You know how eating something
really tasty cheers people up?

00:15:23.884 --> 00:15:25.884
Like the two of you just now!

00:15:25.884 --> 00:15:26.914
Yes.

00:15:27.554 --> 00:15:33.184
I'd like to cook food that
makes people happy.

00:15:33.664 --> 00:15:36.224
Besides, I'm clearly not college material...

00:15:36.494 --> 00:15:38.594
Miss Kawashima, that's wonderful!

00:15:39.134 --> 00:15:42.834
You always make delicious food when
we have cooking practicum!

00:15:43.204 --> 00:15:46.294
I'm sure you'll make a great cook!

00:15:46.544 --> 00:15:49.234
Is that so? Well, thanks.

00:15:50.814 --> 00:15:53.044
I really admire you both.

00:15:54.284 --> 00:16:00.514
Akane-chin and Michi, you both know
what you want to do in life!

00:16:00.994 --> 00:16:02.354
What this "chin" business?

00:16:02.554 --> 00:16:06.584
Well, you should be a bit more
honest with yourself, Wakatake.

00:16:07.364 --> 00:16:09.264
What do you mean?

00:16:09.564 --> 00:16:13.334
If you don't know, then never mind!

00:16:13.834 --> 00:16:16.474
What's that supposed to mean, Akane?

00:16:16.474 --> 00:16:17.434
Oh, so now we're on a first name basis?

00:16:17.434 --> 00:16:18.944
Well, you didn't like "Akane-chin."

00:16:18.944 --> 00:16:19.774
Yeah, well, I'm older than you!

00:16:19.774 --> 00:16:22.074
More honest?
Yeah, well, I'm older than you!

00:16:22.074 --> 00:16:23.174
Akane-tan!

00:16:23.174 --> 00:16:24.614
What's this "tan" business?

00:16:29.184 --> 00:16:30.754
Hey!

00:16:30.754 --> 00:16:32.744
We've been looking for you!

00:16:36.454 --> 00:16:37.824
Let's leave.

00:16:43.664 --> 00:16:45.764
We'd like a word with you.

00:16:45.764 --> 00:16:47.964
We've got unfinished business!

00:16:48.934 --> 00:16:51.164
You want another beat-down?

00:16:58.284 --> 00:17:01.544
Anti-personnel probe,
arriving at target's location.

00:17:02.584 --> 00:17:05.244
Initiating target assessment!

00:17:27.474 --> 00:17:29.034
Commander...

00:17:30.744 --> 00:17:32.734
Why are you doing this?

00:17:49.864 --> 00:17:52.124
You don't know when to quit, do you?

00:17:52.704 --> 00:17:54.104
Damn it!

00:17:59.944 --> 00:18:01.914
I'll call the police!

00:18:09.284 --> 00:18:10.314
Ow-ow-ow-ow!

00:18:10.314 --> 00:18:13.224
Take that! And that!

00:18:13.924 --> 00:18:15.284
Michi!

00:18:16.054 --> 00:18:17.454
Why, you...!

00:18:23.994 --> 00:18:24.664
Shit!

00:18:24.664 --> 00:18:26.434
Hey, come back!

00:18:26.434 --> 00:18:29.174
Owww! Let go!

00:18:29.174 --> 00:18:31.294
Forget them! We'll take her!

00:18:38.444 --> 00:18:39.814
Wakatake!

00:18:40.714 --> 00:18:42.204
Mari!

00:18:44.114 --> 00:18:48.124
Let me go! Let me go! Jerks! Let me out!

00:18:48.124 --> 00:18:49.994
Shut up!

00:18:49.994 --> 00:18:51.784
We'll show you, you brat!

00:18:52.624 --> 00:18:54.284
Target located.

00:18:54.494 --> 00:18:56.364
Currently in transit at low velocity.

00:18:57.294 --> 00:18:59.024
Retrieve her.

00:18:59.364 --> 00:19:01.404
Alive, if possible.

00:19:01.404 --> 00:19:03.064
Roger!

00:19:06.704 --> 00:19:10.244
What are we doing here? What do you want?!

00:19:10.244 --> 00:19:13.514
You never shut up, do you, missy?

00:19:15.914 --> 00:19:17.584
Let go, you little...

00:19:17.584 --> 00:19:19.744
Hey, quit that!

00:19:37.134 --> 00:19:39.104
What is that?

00:20:04.764 --> 00:20:06.354
No!

00:20:07.804 --> 00:20:10.104
No! Let me go!

00:20:10.334 --> 00:20:12.104
Let me go!

00:20:56.854 --> 00:20:58.084
It's you...

00:20:59.054 --> 00:21:00.354
Just in time!

00:21:09.964 --> 00:21:14.804
Summon the commanders of all ships apart
from Ship Five for an urgent message!

00:21:15.204 --> 00:21:19.034
This vessel will now return to Trench One.

00:21:20.804 --> 00:21:22.434
Roger.

00:21:45.604 --> 00:21:49.294
Why were you dressed like that?!

00:21:51.074 --> 00:21:54.044
Why didn't you come rescue me sooner!?

00:21:56.274 --> 00:21:57.714
I'm sorry.

00:21:58.514 --> 00:22:00.104
I was so scared...

00:22:01.084 --> 00:22:03.074
I was so scared!

00:22:16.964 --> 00:22:18.454
So warm...

00:22:18.664 --> 00:22:20.934
What's that supposed to mean?

00:22:21.904 --> 00:22:24.994
You stupid... stupid...

00:22:25.644 --> 00:22:27.934
Stupid...

00:22:30.944 --> 00:22:32.184
Wakatake!

00:22:32.184 --> 00:22:33.844
Mari!

00:22:37.154 --> 00:22:38.184
Mari!

00:22:38.184 --> 00:22:39.674
Hagino?

00:22:45.094 --> 00:22:50.264
Miss Kawashima? Before, when you said Mari
should be more honest with herself...

00:22:50.264 --> 00:22:52.264
Oh, that?

00:22:52.264 --> 00:22:57.294
I meant that Wakatake's totally
fascinated by Senkoji.

00:22:57.874 --> 00:23:01.964
Who knows why they're
so drawn to each other...

00:23:03.574 --> 00:23:07.774
The fact that they're drawn to each
other is the important part, I guess.

00:23:09.754 --> 00:23:14.684
That's true. That's the important part!

00:23:29.534 --> 00:23:37.004
Futari narande te o tsunaida sora ni

00:23:37.814 --> 00:23:47.854
Mirai kasane chikau ano chiheisen

00:23:47.854 --> 00:23:55.524
Kaze ga yasashiku fuki nuketeku youni

00:23:56.234 --> 00:24:04.104
Bokura asu e toketetta

00:24:04.704 --> 00:24:08.314
Nagarete ku toki wa tada

00:24:08.314 --> 00:24:13.644
Shizuka ni kimi wo mimamotte

00:24:13.844 --> 00:24:17.584
Kanashimi mo "Sayonara" mo

00:24:17.584 --> 00:24:23.084
Aoi namida mo tsuyosa ni naru

00:24:24.424 --> 00:24:28.734
Bokura yume kakeru tsubomi

00:24:28.734 --> 00:24:33.564
Kotae sagashi ikiteku

00:24:33.564 --> 00:24:37.874
Hokori takaku saku hana ni

00:24:37.874 --> 00:24:43.574
Itsuka wa nareru to shinjiteta

00:24:43.574 --> 00:24:47.534
In the blue dreams!

00:25:02.134 --> 00:25:06.364
Akane struggles with the loss of parental ties.

00:25:06.664 --> 00:25:12.164
Hagino is unable to comprehend those ties,
and Mari struggles to bridge the gap.

00:25:13.674 --> 00:25:20.514
Meanwhile, an ally ship, Kelbil, attacks Blue.

00:25:22.814 --> 00:25:28.014
Next time on Blue Drop: Garden Verbena.
